-  "quan.pho.greet": "Quit your job to learn cooking? Bold. Phở is lesson one — make a decent bowl before you talk about the road.",
-  "quan.pho.dare": "Work the shift properly. Earn the stars and I'll give you the real recipe to take home.",
-  "quan.mon-kho.greet": "You're the one who quit the office to learn cooking? I follow you online!",
-  "quan.mon-kho.dare": "Bún chả and bún đậu trays have to look good for the photo. Herbs first, bún after — remember.",
-  "quan.cha-ca.greet": "This shop is a hundred years old, kid. Chả cá has no fixed order, but all seven parts must be there.",
-  "quan.cha-ca.dare": "Be neat, be quick. I'm not in a hurry, but the customers are.",
-  "quan.hai-phong.greet": "Made it to Hải Phòng, huh. Red noodles, fish cake, crab broth — port food has to be bold.",
-  "quan.hai-phong.dare": "I drive all day, ten minutes for breakfast. Fast and right, kid.",
-  "quan.bun-rieu.greet": "Came all the way from the north to learn riêu? Sit down, let me tell you how this pot is made.",
-  "quan.bun-rieu.dare": "Crab stock, blood, water — in that order or the broth clouds. One slip and the whole pot is muddy.",
-  "quan.bun-bo.greet": "Bún bò Huế must be spicy, must smell of lemongrass, must be red with annatto. Can you handle spicy?",
-  "quan.bun-bo.dare": "Most toppings on this road. Remember them all and I'm impressed.",
-  "quan.chao.greet": "Sài Gòn wakes early, kid. The porridge pot boils at four a.m.",
-  "quan.chao.dare": "Porridge takes long — start before anyone orders. Make them wait and they're gone.",
-  "quan.khai-vi.greet": "Summer rolls and spring rolls — every foreigner loves them. Learn these and you can go anywhere.",
-  "quan.khai-vi.dare": "Roll tight, fry on low. Two jobs, two rhythms — do them side by side to keep up.",
-  "scene.tap": "tap to continue",
-  "scene.owner": "Owner",
-  "menu.intro": "Replay the intro",
-  "intro.1": "11 pm. The hundredth spreadsheet. The third cup of instant noodles this week. What am I doing?",
-  "intro.2": "An old photo on the phone: the phở stall at the alley, the old lady ladling steaming broth. I used to love that smell.",
-  "intro.3": "Next morning: a resignation letter on the desk, next to a pair of chopsticks. A backpack, a mat, and one reason — go learn to cook this whole country.",
-  "intro.4": "From Hà Nội all the way south. Ask into every kitchen, work the line until the owner hands over the recipe. The trip begins.",
-  "codex.pho-tai-dap.story": "Beef pounded with ginger until tender and fragrant, then cooked by the hot broth at the moment of ladling.",
-  "codex.pho-tai-dap.eat": "Ladle broth at a rolling boil so the beef is just done.",
-  "codex.banh-hoi-thit-heo.story": "Bánh hỏi are ultra-fine vermicelli pressed into sheets, brushed with scallion oil and eaten with boiled or roast pork — a feast dish of the central and south-central coast.",
-  "codex.banh-hoi-thit-heo.eat": "Wrap bánh hỏi, pork and herbs in rice paper or eat as is, dipped in sweet-sour fish sauce.",
-  "codex.pho-dac-biet.story": "'Special' means the bowl has everything the shop offers: rare beef, brisket, tripe, meatballs.",
-  "codex.pho-dac-biet.eat": "Dip the meatballs in hoisin mixed with sriracha.",
-  "codex.bun-ca-hai-phong.story": "Crisp fried fish, fish cake, water celery and dill on a clear fish-bone broth — a familiar Hải Phòng breakfast.",
-  "codex.bun-ca-hai-phong.eat": "Dill goes in last for the aroma; dip the fish in chili fish sauce.",
-  "codex.chao-suon.story": "Silky porridge from finely ground rice, pork ribs simmered to falling apart, with dough sticks, scallion and pepper — a Hanoi breakfast.",
-  "codex.chao-suon.eat": "Pepper, scallion, eaten hot with dough sticks.",
-  "codex.pho-sot-vang.story": "Sốt vang is French-style beef braised in red wine, 'Vietnamized' by Hanoians and ladled over pho as its own dish.",
-  "codex.pho-sot-vang.eat": "Usually eaten with bread or pho, few herbs.",
-  "codex.pho-suon-tai.story": "Beef ribs simmered tender in the broth pot, served with rare beef — the filling pho for working folks.",
-  "codex.pho-suon-tai.eat": "Gnaw the ribs first, then the pho.",
-  "codex.bun-ga-nuong.story": "Dry noodle bowl with lemongrass-marinated grilled chicken, fresh herbs, peanuts and fried shallots.",
-  "codex.bun-ga-nuong.eat": "Pour on sweet-sour fish sauce and toss.",
-  "codex.bun-bo-hue.story": "Broth simmered from beef bones and pork knuckle, fragrant with lemongrass and fermented shrimp, red with annatto chili oil. Thick round noodles are the Huế signature.",
-  "codex.bun-bo-hue.eat": "Shaved banana blossom, sprouts, herbs; squeeze lime, add sa tế chili.",
-  "codex.bun-dau-mam-tom.story": "A Hanoi sidewalk lunch: pressed bún, crisp fried tofu, pork sausage, herbs — everything orbits the cup of shrimp paste.",
-  "codex.bun-dau-mam-tom.eat": "Whisk shrimp paste with sugar, lime, chili and hot oil until foamy, then dip each item.",
-  "codex.bun-nem-cua-thit-nuong-tom-nuong.story": "Southern-style dry noodle bowl: bún, herbs, pickles, crab spring rolls, grilled pork, shrimp — dressed with sweet-sour fish sauce.",
-  "codex.bun-nem-cua-thit-nuong-tom-nuong.eat": "Toss from the bottom up before eating.",
-  "codex.pho-tai-nam.story": "Pho is the national noodle soup, born in the north in the early 20th century. Tái nạm is the classic: rare beef cooked by hot broth, brisket simmered soft.",
-  "codex.pho-tai-nam.eat": "Lime, fresh chili, herbs; in the south add sprouts and hoisin.",
-  "codex.pho-ga.story": "Hanoi chicken pho: free-range chicken, clear broth, fragrant with charred ginger. Born when beef was scarce in the 1940s.",
-  "codex.pho-ga.eat": "Add shredded lime leaf, pepper, lime and chili.",
-  "codex.cha-gio-viet-nam.story": "Chả giò in the south, nem rán in the north: rice paper rolled around pork, shrimp, glass noodles and wood ear, fried golden.",
-  "codex.cha-gio-viet-nam.eat": "Wrap in lettuce and herbs, dip in sweet-sour fish sauce.",
-  "codex.bun-rieu-cua.story": "Riêu is pounded, strained field-crab, cooked with gently tart tomato. A humble dish found in all three regions, each with its own twist.",
-  "codex.bun-rieu-cua.eat": "Add shrimp paste, split water spinach, sprouts and Vietnamese balm.",
-  "codex.banh-da-cua.story": "Red-brown bánh đa noodles are a Hải Phòng specialty; field-crab broth, fish cake, beef in betel leaf, water spinach — the port city's 'everything' bowl.",
-  "codex.banh-da-cua.eat": "With chili jam, fresh herbs and a touch of shrimp paste.",
